*> PLB-K005 batch-io-in-cics: COBOL file statements and ACCEPT of input
*> in a program with EXEC CICS commands.
IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. CICSBAT.
ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
FILE-CONTROL.
    SELECT AUDIT-FILE ASSIGN TO AUDITDD.
DATA DIVISION.
FILE SECTION.
FD  AUDIT-FILE.
01  AUDIT-REC               PIC X(80).
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01  WS-TODAY                PIC 9(8).
01  WS-USER                 PIC X(8).
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    *> Fine: the clock.
    ACCEPT WS-TODAY FROM DATE YYYYMMDD
    *> Reported: no SYSIN, and no COBOL files, in a CICS task.
    ACCEPT WS-USER
    OPEN EXTEND AUDIT-FILE
    WRITE AUDIT-REC
    CLOSE AUDIT-FILE
    EXEC CICS RETURN END-EXEC.

IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
PROGRAM-ID. BATCHLOG.
DATA DIVISION.
WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
01  WS-LINE                 PIC X(80).
PROCEDURE DIVISION.
    *> Fine: a nested program without CICS commands of its own.
    ACCEPT WS-LINE
    GOBACK.
END PROGRAM BATCHLOG.
END PROGRAM CICSBAT.
